session Covariation_Constrained_Martingales = Path_Space_Operations +
  description "
    Martingale laws on the space of continuous paths whose covariation has
    its density in a given set S of matrices, and the minimum-exit-time
    problem over them, with S as a parameter.  The class is closed under
    weak limits and tight when S is closed with a norm and a diagonal
    bound, so it is weakly compact; in particular it is relatively compact
    for a bounded and compact for a compact set of positive semidefinite
    matrices.  Laws of Brownian motion pushed through a matrix with
    covariation rate in S witness that the class is nonempty.  The class is
    closed under shortening the horizon and under pasting at a time, for
    convex S; the value is upper semicontinuous and attained, with a
    measurable optimizer.  Conditioning on the past at a stopping time and
    the additive glue at a stopping time give the dynamic programming
    principle for the value, with attainment, at a deterministic time and at
    a stopping time.
  "
  options [document = pdf, document_output = "output"]
  sessions
    Wiener_Measure
  theories
    Covariation_Class_Limits
    Covariation_Class_Tightness
    Covariation_Class_Shift
    Covariation_Class_Witness
    Covariation_Class_Pasting
    Covariation_Class_Optimizer
    Dynamic_Programming_Pasting
    Dynamic_Programming_Conditioning
    Dynamic_Programming_Stopping_Clauses
    Dynamic_Programming_Additive_Glue
    Dynamic_Programming_Delayed_Class
    Dynamic_Programming_Assembly
    Dynamic_Programming_Principle
  theories [document = false]
    No_Paper_Ancestor
